---
import ProsePage from '../components/ProsePage.astro';
import { company } from '../data/company';
---

<ProsePage
  path="/editorial-policy/"
  crumbLabel="Editorial policy"
  eyebrow="How we write"
  heading="Editorial policy"
  lead={`This SDF Clothing editorial policy explains who writes the pages on ${company.officialDomain}, where our facts come from, how we use AI tools and how we keep everything up to date.`}
>
  <h2>Who writes our pages</h2>
  <p>
    Pages are written and maintained by the merchandising team at {company.legalName} in {company.address.locality}, the same people who quote, sample and run
    production orders. Technical topics such as fabrics, sampling and inspection are checked by staff who handle them on the production floor. Pages are
    reviewed before publication by {company.founder.name}, {company.founder.jobTitle}, who founded the company in {company.foundingYear}.
  </p>

  <h2>Where our facts come from</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Our own terms and prices</strong>, such as minimum order, lead times, payment schedule and the price index, come from company records. They are
      kept in one place, so every page shows the same figure.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Industry figures</strong>, such as export statistics and trade rules, come from official or primary sources, including Bangladesh's Export
      Promotion Bureau, Eurostat and the US Office of Textiles and Apparel, and name the source and date.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Regulations and duty rates</strong> change often. We explain the principle and ask you to confirm the current rate with your customs broker.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How we use AI tools</h2>
  <p>
    We use AI tools to help research, draft and structure pages. Facts are never taken from an AI tool: every figure comes from our company records or a cited
    source, and a member of our team reviews each page before it is published.
  </p>

  <h2>What we do not do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We do not publish reviews, testimonials or case studies without the customer's permission.</li>
    <li>We do not change a page's date unless its content has been meaningfully updated.</li>
    <li>We do not publish claims we cannot back up on request.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How often we review content</h2>
  <p>
    Prices and terms are reviewed at least every three months. Product and service pages are reviewed every six months, and guides every twelve months, or
    sooner when rules or data change. Each page shows the date it was last updated.
  </p>

  <h2>Report an error</h2>
  <p>
    If you find something wrong or out of date, tell us through our <a href={company.contactPath}>contact form</a> with the page address. We correct confirmed errors
    and update the date on the page.
  </p>
</ProsePage>
